## Why This Is Asked

This question probes how to architect a multi-IdP authentication layer that scales across tenants, focusing on correctness and operational concerns rather than theory.

## Key Concepts

- OIDC token validation (audience, issuer, nonce) and SAML assertion validation (Signature, Conditions, AudienceRestriction)
- JWKS rotation and per-tenant metadata caching
- JWT binding with per-device nonce and PKCE for public clients
- Refresh token rotation and reuse detection
- Scalable, cross-region revocation and token introspection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token issuance example
function issueJwt(payload, kid) {
  const header = { alg: 'RS256', kid };
  const token = jwt.sign(payload, getPrivateKeyForKid(kid), {
    algorithm: 'RS256',
    header,
    expiresIn: '15m'
  });
  return token;
}
```

